{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0186aMS5rs5TLfLN5weTVcS5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Test-only utilities split out of [`crate::utils`].\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Contents:\n4\t//!\n5\t//! * **Deterministic test RNG** (`test_random`, `test_random_bytes`,\n6\t//!   `test_uniform_random`, `test_gauss_random`,\n7\t//!   `test_poisson_random`) — picoquic uses these to make\n8\t//!   simulator runs reproducible.  The production RNG\n9\t//!   (`crate::utils::uniform_random`) stays in `utils.rs`.\n10\t//!\n11\t//! * **Network simulator** (`TestSimPacket`, `TestSimLink`,\n12\t//!   `TestAqm`, `JitterMode`) — the in-process sim-link used by\n13\t//!   the test suite to exercise the QUIC stack without real sockets.\n14\t//!   The C bodies live in `picoquictest/sim_link.c`.\n15\t//!\n16\t//! * **TLS API test context** (`TestTlsApiCtx`, `TestApiStreamDesc`,\n17\t//!   `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex`, etc.) — translation of the\n18\t//!   `picoquic_test_tls_api_ctx_t` infrastructure and the helpers\n19\t//!   declared in `picoquictest/picoquictest_internal.h`.\n20\t//!\n21\t//! * **Test-fixture certificate / SNI constants** — paths to PEM\n22\t//!   files baked into the test tree (`certs/...`).\n23\t//!\n24\t//! All `pub` items in this module ride on the parent's\n25\t//! `#[cfg(test)]` gate, so they don't bloat the production build.\n26\t\n27\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n28\t\n29\tuse crate::internal::{Connection, MAX_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT, SackList, Version, format_ack_frame};\n30\tuse crate::tp::TransportParameters;\n31\tuse crate::{ConnectionId, Instant, MAX_PACKET_SIZE, PacketContext, Quic, RESET_SECRET_SIZE};\n32\t\n33\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n34\t// Deterministic test RNG.\n35\t//\n36\t// The production `uniform_random` reads from the platform RNG\n37\t// (and stays in `crate::utils`).  These deterministic helpers\n38\t// thread their state through the explicit `&mut u64` context\n39\t// so simulator runs reproduce bit-for-bit.\n40\t\n41\t/// Deterministic test RNG: advance the 64-bit context and return\n42\t/// the new value.  C: `uint64_t test_random(uint64_t*\n43\t/// random_context)`.\n44\tpub fn test_random(random_context: &mut u64) -> u64 {\n45\t    *random_context = random_context.wrapping_add(0x9e3779b97f4a7c15);\n46\t    let mut z = *random_context;\n47\t    z = (z ^ (z >> 30)).wrapping_mul(0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9u64);\n48\t    z = (z ^ (z >> 27)).wrapping_mul(0x94d049bb133111ebu64);\n49\t    z ^ (z >> 31)\n50\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da743372-a94e-4c3a-8252-a357471bf140","uuid":"5fb469b7-671a-46a0-8c61-28539b4262a1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T10:15:38.793Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs","content":"//! Test-only utilities split out of [`crate::utils`].\n//!\n//! Contents:\n//!\n//! * **Deterministic test RNG** (`test_random`, `test_random_bytes`,\n//!   `test_uniform_random`, `test_gauss_random`,\n//!   `test_poisson_random`) — picoquic uses these to make\n//!   simulator runs reproducible.  The production RNG\n//!   (`crate::utils::uniform_random`) stays in `utils.rs`.\n//!\n//! * **Network simulator** (`TestSimPacket`, `TestSimLink`,\n//!   `TestAqm`, `JitterMode`) — the in-process sim-link used by\n//!   the test suite to exercise the QUIC stack without real sockets.\n//!   The C bodies live in `picoquictest/sim_link.c`.\n//!\n//! * **TLS API test context** (`TestTlsApiCtx`, `TestApiStreamDesc`,\n//!   `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex`, etc.) — translation of the\n//!   `picoquic_test_tls_api_ctx_t` infrastructure and the helpers\n//!   declared in `picoquictest/picoquictest_internal.h`.\n//!\n//! * **Test-fixture certificate / SNI constants** — paths to PEM\n//!   files baked into the test tree (`certs/...`).\n//!\n//! All `pub` items in this module ride on the parent's\n//! `#[cfg(test)]` gate, so they don't bloat the production build.\n\nuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n\nuse crate::internal::{Connection, MAX_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT, SackList, Version, format_ack_frame};\nuse crate::tp::TransportParameters;\nuse crate::{ConnectionId, Instant, MAX_PACKET_SIZE, PacketContext, Quic, RESET_SECRET_SIZE};\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Deterministic test RNG.\n//\n// The production `uniform_random` reads from the platform RNG\n// (and stays in `crate::utils`).  These deterministic helpers\n// thread their state through the explicit `&mut u64` context\n// so simulator runs reproduce bit-for-bit.\n\n/// Deterministic test RNG: advance the 64-bit context and return\n/// the new value.  C: `uint64_t test_random(uint64_t*\n/// random_context)`.\npub fn test_random(random_context: &mut u64) -> u64 {\n    *random_context = random_context.wrapping_add(0x9e3779b97f4a7c15);\n    let mut z = *random_context;\n    z = (z ^ (z >> 30)).wrapping_mul(0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9u64);\n    z = (z ^ (z >> 27)).wrapping_mul(0x94d049bb133111ebu64);\n    z ^ (z >> 31)\n}","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4492}}}
