n-UTF8 content versus `&str` to follow the module's existing conventions like `parse_hexa`, and I'm leaning toward `&str` for consistency with the codebase.\n\nFor `picoquic_set_abs_delay`, the C function updates a timespec in place by adding a delay to the current wall clock time—in Rust I can return `SystemTime::now() + Duration::from_micros(microsec_wait)` since this Unix-only helper is only used in the pthread timed lock wrapper and the stdlib types are the approved mapping.\n\nNow I need to check how the existing bbr.rs handles the `Connection` dependency in `start_round` before tackling `BBRAdaptLowerBoundsFromCongestion` and `BBRAdaptUpperBounds`.\n\nLet me look at `BBRInflightWithBw` next, which the C code references but I haven't found in my bbr.rs review yet.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2075,"cache_read_input_tokens":93476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2075},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da743372-a94e-4c3a-8252-a357471bf140","uuid":"81d41cf2-95d2-4de7-b811-0fa5f45956fa"}
